:<!--1-second delay-->
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Heh, that's alright. In these times of conflict, for the sake of utmost safety, it is only right that the Alliance steps forward to mediate on behalf of the Astral Express. We must not allow you to take unnecessary risks.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Furthermore, despite the IPC's eagerness for success, it prioritizes "peace" above all, and The Family, trapped though it may be, professes a desire for "Harmony." The Alliance has always won people over with reason. I firmly believe both parties can indeed put aside their differences and come to a peaceful agreement.
:'''Himeko:''' The general possesses a deep understanding of the greater good. With the Xianzhou Alliance mediating, peace for Penacony is within reach.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' You flatter me! But ultimately, it's been all down to the Express. Without your efforts, this Sweetdream Paradise would have been claimed by the last remnants of "Order" before there was even a shot at peace...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Well would you look at that. Here comes the big hero.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It was nothing, really.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Hahaha, here's the Galactic Baseballer &mdash; the paragon of both heroism and humility!
::I do what I can.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Hahaha, if it isn't the Galactic Baseballer &mdash; a true hero who dares to take action!
::Lemme guess, you were thinking about me... again?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I do what I can.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Hahaha, if it isn't the Galactic Baseballer &mdash; a true hero who dares to take action!
::Lemme guess, you were thinking about me... again?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Lemme guess, you were thinking about me... again?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Hahaha, if it isn't the Galactic Baseballer &mdash; a hero with unparalleled insight!
:'''Welt:''' (Trailblazer), are you okay? I heard you couldn't wake up. Are you feeling unwell?
:'''March 7th:''' Don't worry, Mr. Yang. There's nothing wrong with {{MC|м=him|ж=her}}, {{MC|м=he|ж=she}} practically burned through a lifetime's worth of jokes on the way here.
:'''March 7th:''' What about you, Mr. Yang? I heard that even Miss Robin wasn't spared, and that guy locked you both up...
:'''Welt:''' It's a long story... but, at least Mr. Sunday took it easy on us.
:'''Welt:''' He used an ability called "tuning" to connect our consciousnesses with his. In other words, he imprisoned us within his consciousness.
:'''Welt:''' Thanks to General Jing Yuan's destruction of the Harmonious Choir, we were able to escape.
:'''March 7th:''' Ah, he used that "tuning" on us, too! Does that mean that we were almost imprisoned as well...?
:'''Himeko:''' I can confidently say now, he was truly after a fair fight with us. Had he wanted, he could have easily taken us down... without so much as lifting a finger.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Speaking of the Oak Family head... Where is he now?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' It's complicated, but in a nutshell, he's now the former Oak Family head.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' The IPC has named him the key figure in The Family's Penacony split, citing a threat to Cosmic peace. He must represent The Family and answer for the unrest caused. His trial is set to take place at Pier Point.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' The Family quickly labeled him and the remnants of the Order as enemies, declaring the turmoil an internal rebellion. This move effectively barred the IPC from intervening in "Family affairs" on both moral and rational grounds.
:'''Welt:''' Everyone really has their own agenda after all...
:'''March 7th:''' Then... what's going to happen to Miss Robin? She and Sunday won't be able to deny their involvement in the Charmony Festival, they're siblings after all...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' ...
:'''March 7th:''' Why the sigh, General?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' I can only say that this incident is an unexpected mess for the girl. The Alliance will try to persuade The Family to consider this matter carefully during mediation.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' It's time, everyone. The IPC's key members and I have agreed to consult one another before the upcoming negotiation. Do any of you wish to sit in?
:'''Himeko:''' Given the general's invitation and the matter's significance to the universe, the Crew will naturally accept. However, if the IPC has any reservations...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Why of course you're welcome! They've mentioned that your team is a trusted ally of the IPC in Penacony, so there's no reason not to welcome you.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Besides, if there can be reliable observers from the Astral Express present, discussions will go more smoothly. So, what do you all think?
:'''Himeko:''' Well then, we shall oblige.
:'''March 7th:''' ...I'm a kind of allergic to those types of situations. I think I'll just head back to my room and start packing.
:'''Welt:''' Not to worry. Himeko and I will take care of things.
:'''Dan Heng:''' I'm afraid I'll also have to return to the Express first. The conductor is worried about us. It's best I go and explain the situation.
:'''Himeko:''' Thank you. What about you, (Trailblazer)? Will you join Welt and me, or have you got other plans?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'll go with Miss Himeko.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha, great.
::I HAVE TO help March pack her suitcase...
::'''March 7th:''' What? I can pack it myself, you know...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha, if that's the case, our Galactic Baseballer can join us.
::Dunno why, but something tells me I only have one real option here...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I HAVE TO help March pack her suitcase...
::'''March 7th:''' What? I can pack it myself, you know...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha, if that's the case, our Galactic Baseballer can join us.
::Dunno why, but something tells me I only have one real option here...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Dunno why, but something tells me I only have one real option here...
